<div class="blockquote">
<p style="text-align: center;"><strong>INTERVIEW LOG</strong></p>
<hr />
<p><strong>Interviewed:</strong> SCP-5418</p>
<p><strong>Interviewer:</strong> Head Researcher and Director of Site ██ Dr Natalia Fox</p>
<hr />
<p><em>SCP-5418 is seen sitting across the table from Dr Fox with a handcuff.</em></p>
<p><strong>Dr. Fox:</strong> Hello. I’m Head Researcher Dr Natalia Fox, and I’ll be talking to you today.</p>
<p><strong>SCP-5418:</strong> (<em>Stammers in heavy accent</em>) H-Hello. M-My name is Oulen.</p>
<p><strong>Dr. Fox:</strong> Oh, you seem to know English a lot.</p>
<p><strong>SCP-5418:</strong> I-I uh, I was learning English. Um, I hope you can understand.</p>
<p><strong>Dr. Fox:</strong> You're doing fine. Now please tell me when you learned about your ability.</p>
<p><strong>SCP-5418:</strong> Um, it's been a couple of months now, I first learned about it when I was at school, trying to concentrate but it wasn’t working so I just started daydreaming I realized there was snow falling inside the class. My teacher wasn’t present, so I guessed it was her doing it as a special effect for the upcoming Christmas celebration. Later I was walking with my friends when I saw a dead bird. I picked it up and tried to bring it back, but it was already dead, so I placed it back on the ground when the bird started to turn. It came back. I brought it back. That’s when I learned about this ability.</p>
<p><strong>Dr. Fox:</strong> I see, So your friends had seen the instance of your ability. Thanks for telling me that.</p>
<p><strong>SCP-5418:</strong> Is that a bad thing?</p>
<p><strong>Dr. Fox:</strong> Yes. The knowledge of your anomalous ability would be too much for your friends.</p>
<p><strong>SCP-5418:</strong> Why would that be? I know them, they won't tell anyone about me.</p>
<p><strong>Dr. Fox:</strong> That is a chance we can't take XXXX.</p>
<p><strong>SCP-5418:</strong> Can I at least leave?</p>
<p><strong>Dr. Fox:</strong> No, 5418, you will not be able to leave. You’re dangerous to outside people we are protecting. We even safeguarding you, from them as well.</p>
<p><strong>SCP-5418:</strong> Should I be thankful for that?</p>
<p><strong>Dr. Fox:</strong> You can think whatever you want as long as your not hurting anyone.</p>
<p><strong>SCP-5418:</strong> What will happen to me? Will, I able to do whatever I want inside the cell? Can I roam around the facility? I'm somewhat claustrophobic.</p>
<p><strong>Dr. Fox:</strong> We'll see what we can do with the claustrophobia, so you don't have to worry about that. The second, you wouldn't roam around the facility as it is dangerous to you and others. We need you to stay inside your containment chamber.</p>
<p><em>SCP-5418 nods.</em></p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Close</a></div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Before its containment, SCP-5418 studied at █████ High School, ███████████. Due to the classmates and civilian around SCP-5418 that witnessed its reality-bending ability, they had been tracked and administered Class-A amnestic. Any information involving SCP-5418 has been confiscated and erased from every database.</p>
<p><strong>Addendum 5418.2</strong> Dr Fox had done a series of tests to understand the extent of SCP-XXXX's reality-warping capacity.</p>
