<hr />
<p><strong>Dr. Fox:</strong> How have you been 5418?</p>
<p><strong>SCP-5418:</strong> Good. Umm, they gave me a book. To be honest, I'm not much of a reader. It's kind of lonely inside the cell.</p>
<p><strong>Dr. Fox:</strong> Your English have improved. I guess the book has been good help?</p>
<p><strong>SCP-5418:</strong> Sure, its the only form of entertainment inside these four walls. Also, the guards outside are scared of me, won't even talk to me.</p>
<p><strong>Dr. Fox:</strong> Of course, you are dangerous.</p>
<p><strong>SCP-5418:</strong> Why? What is it about me that is dangerous? Is it because of my power?</p>
<p><strong>Dr. Fox:</strong> (<em>nodding</em>) Yes. Your ability is potent; its enough to rewrite the whole concept of reality.</p>
<p><strong>SCP-5418:</strong> Whoa, that's something. Wait, you won’t kill me, right?</p>
<p><strong>Dr. Fox:</strong> We will see, it depends. I want to ask you a couple of questions. How was your home life before containment? In your private file said your parent died of a car crash.</p>
<p><strong>SCP-5418:</strong> Yeah they died when I was nine or ten. I was in the car at that time when the accident happened. I don’t remember much, really.</p>
<p><strong>Dr. Fox:</strong> Who did you live with after their death?</p>
<p><strong>SCP-5418:</strong> Lived with my uncle. He was a drunken man, and well, he hated me. He used to leave alone basically for days, leaving a small amount of food to&#8230; um, feed me.</p>
<p><strong>Dr. Fox:</strong> I understand, based on the report, he died three days before your containment. What were you doing at that time?</p>
<p><strong>SCP-5418:</strong> Studying, trying to live without a guardian. My mom and dad both had left me money and adding on with my uncle's income. I was pretty rich for my age.</p>
<p><em>SCP-5418 giggles and Dr Fox clears her throat.</em></p>
<p><strong>SCP-5418:</strong> Sorry about that.</p>
<p><strong>Dr. Fox:</strong> Tell me about your parent, were they nice?</p>
<p><strong>SCP-5418:</strong> Well, they were alright, a bit energetic.</p>
<p><strong>Dr. Fox:</strong> I see. I have been observing you for a while now, and it seems you tend to create a carbon-based life from nothing, why is that?</p>
<p><strong>SCP-5418:</strong> I love nature, the fresh air and the wide land's silence are very calming and refreshing for me. When I get out, I'll immediately travel to Mount Bodg and climb the top and scream from the top of my lung. It is a promise.</p>
<p><strong>Dr. Fox:</strong> Right. It sounds like you want to leave. That is not possible, and you will stay here until there's nothing to learn from your ability, then we’ll see whatever you can leave.</p>
<p><strong>SCP-5418:</strong> I doubt that will ever happen to be honest.</p>
<p><strong>Dr. Fox:</strong> (<em>Sighs</em>) Alright, I think this is enough for today.</p>
<p><strong>SCP-5418:</strong> Goodbye.</p>
