<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Incident&nbsp;Report&nbsp;level&nbsp;4&nbsp;clearance:&nbsp;5418.091920</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Incident&nbsp;Report&nbsp;level&nbsp;4&nbsp;clearance:&nbsp;5418.091920</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>INCIDENT REPORT:</strong> On 9/19/2020 sudden Reality distortion formulated by SCP-5418 caused its containment chamber to desert itself in a spatial void with Head Researcher Natalia Fox present in the room.</p>
<p>Following audio recording is from a conversation between SCP-5418 and Dr Fox.</p>
<div class="blockquote">
<hr />
<p style="text-align: center;"><strong>BEGIN LOG</strong></p>
<hr />
<p><em>A heavy metal chair can be heard dragging across the room. Dr Fox's shaky breath can be audible.</em></p>
<p><strong>Dr. Fox:</strong> (<em>Breathing heavily</em>) Wh-What the hell did you do? W-Where are we?</p>
<p><strong>SCP-5418:</strong> You seems to be panicking, I think you should sit down.</p>
<p><strong>Dr. Fox:</strong> Ok, ok. I'll sit down.</p>
<p><strong>SCP-5418:</strong> Let me ask you a question. Would the Foundation really kill me? Please answer it honestly.</p>
<p><strong>Dr. Fox:</strong> Um. W-Well, no. They won't unless you're threatening the secrecy.</p>
<p><strong>SCP-5418:</strong> (<em>Humming</em>) That's good to hear. Have you learned who killed my parents?</p>
<p><strong>Dr. Fox:</strong> Yeah. We already found him.</p>
<p><strong>SCP-5418:</strong> <strong>[Unintelligible]</strong> I miss them. They had a lot of ambition, and then I came around ruined it for them, tied them to each other. Do you know how gruelling it is to be reminded of it for the rest of your childhood? Even after death, they won't leave me alone! that drunken bastard of a man, no wonder he died without dignity.</p>
<p><strong>Dr. Fox:</strong> So&#8230; <strong>[Unintelligible]</strong> <strong>[Audio static]</strong> and you killed your uncle too?</p>
<p><strong>SCP-5418:</strong> (<em>scowls</em>) No, it was his own doing, I had no relation&#8230; on behalf of his death. It just his pathetic self.. being pathetic.</p>
<p><strong>Dr. Fox:</strong> (<em>takes a shaky breath</em>) Y-your going to leave? Even if you do, we will found you.</p>
<p><strong>SCP-5418:</strong> Yes, I’m not tied to anything, and I have nothing to lose. But I doubt you'll get far anyway. Besides, I have already left.</p>
<p><em>Distorted scream can be heard in which the recording ends.</em></p>
</div>
<p>SCP-5418 and the containment cell returned to its location about an hour after it disappeared, but without Dr Fox. The subject proceeded to manifest a bird features resembling an eagle approximately 8,5&#160;m in size and flew to Mountain Altai Tavan Bogd in the straight sector.</p>
<p>During its pursuit, SCP-5418 landed on top of the Mountain Bogd, deformed the bird and sunk itself into the Mountain afterwards. MTF-Omega-12 (&quot;Achilles Heels&quot;) enclosed the area and restricted all activity towards the mountain.</p>
<p>Between 8 am to 8&#160;pm, there was no activity. However, at 9&#160;pm, the ground shook in minor 10 decibels until a cave's entry point had formed on the mountain's skirt.</p>
<p>Subsequently, MTF-Omega-12 entered the cave and explored the unknown sinkhole. They found entirely independent ecosystems made from reality restoration with a high amount of Hume<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-2" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-2')">2</a></sup>. About three hours into the exploration, they found SCP-5418 waiting for them outside of what it seems to be a suburban cabin.</p>
<div class="blockquote">
<p><em>1:1 raises his gun and others followed suit, pointing at SCP-5418. The subject raises its hands in the air.</em></p>
<p><strong>SCP-5418:</strong> Calm the fuck down. I’m not hurting anyone.</p>
<p><strong>1:1:</strong> You are in no condition to order us. So, shut up and let us take you back.</p>
<p><strong>SCP-5418:</strong> That's the thing, I can’t let you do that. I’m free here without any boundaries. So no.</p>
<p><em>1:2 walked closer to 1:1 and whispered into his ear.</em></p>
<p><strong>1:1:</strong> What? Can’t you be serious?</p>
<p><strong>1:2:</strong> They want to negotiate. I suggest we listen.</p>
<p><strong>1:1:</strong> Fucking. Fine, give it to him.</p>
<p><em>1:2 walked towards SCP-5418 and gave him the communicator. The entity takes the device and looks at it.</em></p>
<p><strong>SCP-5418:</strong> (<em>towards the com</em>) The only reason I’m letting this device work is that I know you guys would try to talk to me.</p>
<p><strong>Command:</strong> We want to have diplomatic relations. We know we had been a bit too restrictive, but we cannot let you walk by without proper visualisation.</p>
<p><strong>SCP-5418:</strong> I will let you follow me, but that's it. I’m not leaving this place. If you leave me alone here without bothering me too much, I’ll not cause much trouble for you guys and try to make sure not to show my face to anyone. I am keeping the secrecy.</p>
<p><strong>Command:</strong> And what if you won’t?</p>
<p><strong>SCP-5418:</strong> Take me back. But the same goes for you. Suppose if you don’t keep your promise, then you’re going to have significant trouble coming for you.</p>
<p><strong>1:1:</strong> Is that fucking threat?</p>
<p><strong>SCP-5418:</strong> You can say that. Those who can’t keep their promises are a fucking cowards.</p>
<p><strong>Command:</strong> I reassure you, we’ll keep our promise. Omega-12, return to the base. 1:1, place the tracker.</p>
<p><strong>1:3:</strong> What? No action?</p>
<p><strong>1:4:</strong> Shut up, be glad that thing didn’t attack us the moment we placed one foot here, come on.</p>
<p><em>1:1 walked towards SCP-5418 and jabs a needle up to its arm.</em></p>
<p><strong>1:1:</strong> Don’t take it out and keep your promise.</p>
<p><strong>SCP-5418:</strong> Will do. Goodbye.</p>
<p><strong>Command:</strong> Wait! Dr Fox, bring her back.</p>
<p><strong>SCP-5418:</strong> Ugh fine. Tell her I said I never want to see her again.</p>
<hr />
<p><strong>Closing statement:</strong> The MTF-Omega-12 returned to the base and expressed uproar towards the agreement, as said before SCP-5418 will keep it's a promise as long as we keep ours. Anyone opposed to this notion will be reassigned to a different project.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Dr Fox returns to our reality within 5 hours, with minor psychological damage and bodily wounds. She had been sent to the Foundation rehabilitation centre to recover. SCP-5418 agreed to remain in the underground chamber it created; however, it did not want to be visited and ignored the researchers when establishing communication.</p>
<p>Subsequently, on 3/02/2021 SCP-5418 went permanently silent and ceased to be visible inside of the cave. No thermal imagery shows its current location; thus, no communication devices had worked since the cave's inception. Regardless SCP-5418 still resides inside the cave as motion sensor revealed the subject roaming the location in pattern. Albeit the tracking device placed within SCP-5418’s hand had worked significantly less than as expected, the only way to track the subject is when it's inactive during the nights.</p>
